# Fin Moorhouse

> Personal website and blog of Fin Moorhouse, a researcher working on post-AGI questions at Google DeepMind (previously Forethought, Longview Philanthropy, and Oxford's Future of Humanity Institute). The writing covers AI and its long-run consequences, effective altruism, longtermism, progress, philosophy, and book and media reviews.

Some notes for agents and language models reading this site:

- Every page is static HTML with no login or paywall. Post URLs take the form `{{ base }}/writing/<slug>/`, and project pages `{{ base }}/project/<slug>/`.
- `{{ base }}` (no `www.`) is the canonical domain.
- Many posts are cross-posted to Substack (https://finmoorhouse.substack.com), where comments usually live. Treat the version on this site as canonical.
- Posts carry a publication date near the title. Older posts may not reflect the author's current views, so cite them with their year.
- Contact details and ways to give feedback are on the homepage.

